# November 18, 2026: Washington County, Minnesota (the St. Croix valley from Scandia down to Stillwater and Oak Park
# Heights), region mn, drawn at random by tools/choose.py. First real pass in Minnesota (only Mill Ruins Park was on the map).
# Facts come from sources opened in this session: Wikipedia read as raw text (wiki_raw.py), the Washington County
# Historical Society's site pages, the Minnesota Historical Society's Marine Mill pages, Minnesota DNR trail and wayside
# pages, MnDOT's historic-bridge and historic-roadside pages, Washington County's courthouse page, the Gammelgården
# Museum's own pages, the Arcola Mills Historic Foundation's visit page, and HMdb marker texts, all read through
# tools/page.py. Where a managing body's page gave no hours the access note says "hours not checked".
# Brick values: from the sources' words about what each place is built of, or from a picture opened with
# tools/brick.py look ('Washington County Courthouse 2020.jpg': red brick walls on a limestone base; 'Hay Lake School.jpg': red
# brick schoolhouse; 'Isaac Staples Sawmill.jpg': limestone powerhouse and stack beside the metal-clad factory, no brick seen;
# 'Phil\'s Tara Hideaway 2017.jpg': log walls, one small red brick chimney top and one fieldstone chimney). '?' where neither
# settled it (the Boom Site, where little is left; no picture was opened).
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
BATCH={'key':'mn_dzwh','label':'Washington County, Minnesota: St. Croix lumber towns, Stillwater and Scandia','added':'2026-11-18 19:59'}
